{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"P1 recurrence evidence: after the earlier mirror-fetch/buildkit-prune repair and close, Gerrit object-store loss recurred. At 2026-09-08 ~04:45 UTC, rebased Gerrit change 2819 PS3 push for complex-sassy-blackfly failed with `remote unpack failed: error Missing blob ef992016d5f84faddb05a9a086341141a7aeebab` / `remote rejected HEAD -> refs/for/main (n/a (unpacker error))`. Per blackfly instructions I waited a bounded 10 minutes and retried once; the retry failed with the same missing blob. The blob was present when 2819 PS2 pushed successfully at 2026-09-08 04:05:48 UTC and PS2 received LLM-Review+1 at 04:14:48 and Verified+1 at 04:31:31, then Submit hit a rebase conflict and the rebased PS3 push exposed the missing blob. Beginning repair with EBS snapshot backup before touching Gerrit repo objects; will not restart Gerrit or touch unrelated git data beyond the validated mirror-fetch recovery."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788847052167434001,"uuid":"ba756ea9-3d79-4387-b4d1-f93f7f455920"}